  "notes": "LINKS-1. Shared link-detection and host-local rewrite vectors; omodachi-ios (LinkDetector) and Odomo (lib/links.js) must produce exactly these. Matching, left to right, first alternative wins: a link starts at the beginning of the text or right after whitespace or one of ( [ { < \" ' ` = ; URL = https?:// then [^\\s<>\"'`]+ ; PATH = either (~|.|..) then / (not followed by / or whitespace) then [A-Za-z0-9._~@%+=,/:#-]+, or a bare / (not followed by / or whitespace) then the same characters, at least one of which is another / or a . (so </b> and </script> are not paths) ; BARE (mirror only) = [A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9._-]*\\.<known extension, any case> not followed by [A-Za-z0-9_/-]. Then trailing . , ; : ! ? are dropped, and so is a trailing ) ] } that has no opener inside the link, repeatedly. `mirror` = plain terminal text (Herdr mirror): URL, PATH, BARE. `prose` = an agent message's plain text: URL and PATH only. `host_local` and `rewrite` use `roads` = host-roads.json plus the short name (first label of the .local / MagicDNS name). A rewrite keeps scheme, port, path, query and fragment; for http it prefers an IP road (no name lookup, nothing for a browser to try upgrading to https first; measured on iOS 27 both http://<name>.ts.net:port and the IP load in the Safari view): the current road if it is an IP, else the first tailnet IPv4 on a tailnet road, else the first LAN IPv4; for https the current road as it is.",
